{"name":"Magma","hex":"#ff4e01","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magma","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of molten silicate rock, crystals, and gas within the earth, which may be erupted as lava or cool in place to form igneous intrusions.","A basic algebraic structure consisting of a set equipped with a single binary operation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magma"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magma","blocks":[{"text":"Magma is the molten or semi-molten natural material from which all igneous rocks are formed. Magma is found beneath the surface of the Earth, and evidence of magmatism has also been discovered on other terrestrial planets and some natural satellites. Besides molten rock, magma may also contain suspended crystals and gas bubbles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Earth_Internal_Structure.svg/330px-Earth_Internal_Structure.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magma","wikidata":"Q42278"},{"title":"Magma (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Magma is a French progressive rock band founded in Paris in 1969 by self-taught drummer Christian Vander, who claimed as his inspiration a \"vision of humanity's spiritual and ecological future\" that profoundly disturbed him. The style of progressive rock that Vander developed with Magma is termed \"Zeuhl\" and has been applied to other bands in France operating in the same period, and to some recent Japanese bands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/MAGMA_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg/330px-MAGMA_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magma_(band)","wikidata":"Q914489"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Single_tet.png/120px-Single_tet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai